  worth of stuff out of this notebook so  you're welcome  so what else what other common problems  are there another common well this is a  collection of problems with a common  solution collection of problems is I  don't know what's going wrong with my  manipulate it's turning pink things are  going bad I don't know what to do and  it's giving error messages but this is  manipulate and I don't know anything  about interfaces so help so one of the  very useful things and I have an  anecdote about this that I'll tell in a  moment one very useful thing is in every  manipulate so here's a maple 8 that's  going to break and every manipulate with  default options there is a menu up in  the corner with some controls now some  of these controls are rather flashy  there's one I think that doesn't really  get the attention it deserves and that's  paste snapshot which takes out of the  manipulate the body and all of the local  values of all of the local variables and  produces a new input not a manipulated  input it is a dynamic module input but  it produces a new input that gives you  the ability to dig into this particular  frame of the manipulate and what might  be going on so I used this technique  today today to track down a bug  in somebody else's code so here we have  we see we have exactly the same error  messages in fact even with module  instead of dynamic module still have  error messages but at this point users  might think oh well I'm not in  manipulated anymore I can actually read  this message and make some sense of it  so they'll pause hopefully read the  message say endpoints for y must have  distinct machine pursue oh so we have Y  going from 1 to K and K is 1 ah  so if K we're 1.1 is that is that kind  of fit oh but now X has the same problem  because X goes from 0 to n and n is 0 so  we can't have X going from 0 to 0 or  parametric plot will complain  there we go so this gives a way to drill  down into the problem and and make some  headway and this was supposed to be  marked as bonus so you're welcome so  very common to see pinking as a result  of kernel messages generated during a  dynamic update you see dynamic of 1 over  0 creates a little pink box but it  doesn't show you the message until you  do something take a look at this slide  later to find out what to do about that  ok another category of problems my  manipulate is slow why does the cell  bracket keep lighting up how can I avoid  doing I have I have a manipulate that  shows something that uses a lot of work  and something that needs very little  work when I update this I don't want  this to change how do I do that  and this category of problems each of  each of the solutions I'm about to  describe  can affect any one of that in the  category so this is sort of a mix and  match these are all good techniques to  know so what can I say about the cell  bracket staying lit well we've all  experienced a dynamic that just keeps  running and running and running maybe we  have has anybody in this room  experienced that ok a few so this is  because dynamic tries really hard to  make  or that it always shows you the current  value of an expression and it does that  by remembering all of the symbols that  are involved in that expression and  keeping track of each of them and if any  of those changes it updates the dynamic  it it sends a message that says the  dynamic needs to be updated and this is  very very good and sometimes it's very  useful so for instance here is a  manipulate that I wrote some time ago  that uses a pen to to continue to  continually add to a list iteratively  notice there's no animator in this  manipulate call this is this is driving  itself by virtue of having a variable  whose value is changing inside of  dynamic so this dynamic evaluates it  notices that it depends on the value of  lists the value of lists changes during  this dynamic update and then the system  says hey this dynamic depends on lists  lists changed you need to update and so  this runs and runs and runs and we can  say well don't change lists this time  around because I have this paused when  you're paused then you're not doing any  work list is not changing the updates  not changing okay so sometimes I guess  I'm driving home the point that this  dynamic infinite evaluation and dynamic  is a very very good thing but sometimes  it's too much of a good thing so here is  another example pulled straight off of  community I think where we have a global  value of x that somehow depends on a  local value if manipulate and notice the  SEL bracket at the far side stays lit  indicating that something is happening  over and over and over what is happening  well this manipulate this first argument  to manipulate is wrapped and dynamic  this dynamic depends on the value of X  and X changes during this evaluation so  even if it doesn't actually change it's  being reset to the same thing over and  over and over how does one avoid this  category of problems well there are  several ways one is to specify that I  only want particular symbols to be  tracked  you one can do that and manipulate with  the track symbols option here we specify  a single value a single variable that we  want tracked setting track symbols to  true will cause this to track all local  manipulate variables and only the local  manipulate variables that works in this  case because X is not a local manipulate  variable it's a global variable also  something that can be done is to  localize these variables so they are not  global so here we have X being itself a  local variable in a dynamic module or  for that matter in a module this kind of  nesting is perfectly fine another  problem that I mentioned so here we have  an example of something that takes a  while to evaluate and something that's  drop-dead fast to evaluate and we want  to show them both at the same time in  the same manipulate and so we when  dragging this around the contour plot  gets reevaluated that's fine we let g