at they don't refer to any  they don't have their fingers throughout  all of global and if you really want  this thing to to jump to life when you  open it from a file I would recommend  against using save definitions if you're  if you're loading package files package  symbols because you don't want save  definitions pulling pieces of a package  together and injecting them into an  initialization far better in that case  is to create the initialization manually  with the needs of that package and full  definition ignores protected and read  protected symbols so if you're dealing  with those you're probably fairly  advanced but you you shouldn't be using  save definitions in that case okay more  bonus slide more bonus slide that's all  I have  manipulate is very useful and those are  the problems that I've seen people have  in real life and maybe that addressed  some of the things that people here care  about so thanks very much for your  attention  [Applause]
 

